  "text": "> Method ㆍ write(): Write into the HTML output stream ㆍ element.setAttribute(attribute, value): Change the attribute value of an HTML element * focus(): Sets focus to the current window ㆍ getSelection(): Returns a Selection object representing the range of text selected by the user >» Event (Handler) ㆍ document.getElementByld(id).onclick = function() { code here … } // Adding event handler code to an onclick event > Property ㆍ title: title of the document, <title> tag * location: current location of the web browser * bgColor: background color, “bgcolor” attribute * fgColor: foreground or text color, “text” attribute * linkColor: link color, alinkColor: active link color, vlinkColor: visited link color > Event ㆍ onfocus : an event occurs when an element gets focus * onblur : an event occurs when an object loses focus ㆍ onkeydown: an event occurs when the user is pressing a key ㆍ onkeyup: an event occurs when the user releases a key * onclick : an event occurs when the user clicks on an element ㆍ ondblclick : an event occurs when the user double-clicks on an element * onmousedown: an event occurs when a user presses a mouse button over an element ㆍ onmouseup: an event occurs when a user releases a mouse button over an element",
